Compiling Musl C Library inside /sources

1. Navigate to the sources directory and download the Musl archive:

`cd /sources`
`curl -O https://musl.libc.org/releases/musl-1.2.5.tar.gz`

2. Extract the source tarball and enter the source tree:

`tar -xf musl-1.2.5.tar.gz`
`cd musl-1.2.5`

3. Configure, compile, and install Musl C library:

`./configure --prefix=/usr --syslibdir=/lib`
`make -j$(nproc)`
`make install`

4. Clean up source directory after installation:

`cd /sources`
`rm -rf musl-1.2.5`
